    {{! Preload the two brand faces before the stylesheet link. The @font-face
        rules live inside site.css, so without this the browser cannot even
        discover the fonts until the 93KB sheet has downloaded and parsed:
        measured cold, the font requests started at 762ms, 34ms after first
        contentful paint, so every load painted fallback text first and swapped
        ~250ms later. Preloading moves the fetch to HTML-parse time, in
        parallel with the CSS instead of behind it.
        Only the latin subsets, and only the two faces that paint above the
        fold -- Roboto and Roboto Mono are fallback/code faces whose stand-ins
        are metrically close, and preloading them would just contend for
        bandwidth with the stylesheet.
        crossorigin is required: fonts are always fetched in CORS mode, and a
        preload without it is a separate, unused fetch. }}
    <link rel="preload" href="{{{uiRootPath}}}/font/bangers-latin-400-normal.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preload" href="{{{uiRootPath}}}/font/special-elite-latin-400-normal.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{{uiRootPath}}}/css/site.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{{uiRootPath}}}/css/vendor/tabs.css">
